 "notes": "Conservative 'Solar Axion Basin Limit' (boundary of the light-blue conclusively-excluded region) from Fig. 3 (plotgBasin.pdf in the e-print), recovered from the vector path of the figure. Axis calibration verified against the quoted flux-excess box (m: 0.1-1.5 keV, g_aee: 2.6e-12-3.7e-12). The limit recasts DM axion absorption-line searches (XENON1T S2 and S1+S2, LUX, PandaX-II) via Eq. 28 using the paper's Solar-basin density with the conservative gravitational ejection time tau ~ 1e7 y (Eq. 9); it does not assume axions are dark matter, so no DM-density rescaling applies (dm_density_assumed null). The fiducial and optimistic curves (thick/dashed blue) are presented as 'disfavored'/'conceivable signal' regions, not the headline exclusion. Curve endpoints at g=1e-10 are where the region meets the top of the plotted range; a tiny disconnected sliver near m~34-35 keV barely below 1e-10 was ignored. Underlying DM searches are 90% CL; the paper does not restate a CL for the recast. Masses converted from keV to eV.",
